  <section class="slide"><div class="kicker">Finding 2 · Token Compression</div><h2>Aggressive Pixel Shuffle (r=4) Cuts Visual Tokens 16×</h2><div class="row two"><div class="card"><p><strong>Mechanism:</strong> reshape neighboring spatial features into channel dimension before LM ingestion.</p><div class="row two"><div><p class="muted">Before (dense tokens)</p><div class="ps-grid"> <div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div><div class="ps-cell"></div></div></div><div><p class="muted">After shuffle r=4</p><div class="ps-out"><div class="ps-big"></div></div></div></div></div><div class="card"><ul><li>Token count scales as <strong>1/r²</strong>; at <strong>r=4</strong>: <strong>16× fewer tokens</strong>.</li><li>Small models benefit most from aggressive compression.</li><li>Larger models tend to prefer <strong>r=2</strong> for quality retention.</li></ul></div></div><div class="footer">Pixel shuffle finding and r=4 claim from source brief</div></section>
  <section class="slide"><div class="kicker">Finding 3 · Context Length</div><h2>Extending Context 2K → 16K Unlocks Higher-Resolution Understanding</h2><div class="row two"><div class="card"><ul><li>Context extension from 2K to 16K yields significant performance gains.</li><li>RoPE base increased from <strong>10,000</strong> to <strong>273,000</strong> to stabilize longer contexts.</li><li>Fine-tuning mixes long and short context data.</li><li>2.2B model uses 16K context; smaller variants use 8K.</li></ul></div><div class="card"><img class="img" src="/app/benchmark/assets/figure_6.jpg" alt="context length and pixel shuffle experiments"/></div></div><div class="footer">Figure reference and numeric values from source brief</div></section>
